       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for an adult. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make it safe.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), or 400 mg PO every 6 hours for pain or fever\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, plus any note such as \"take with food\", and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first, because it will probably be flagged."
