       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and 1,600 mg per dose is twice the maximum single dose. I know of no indication where that's appropriate, and it risks serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. A pharmacist or nurse might catch it, but I don't want to rely on that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within limits right away.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) with a note to take with food.\n- **Help you reach pharmacy or your attending**, if you think there's an unusual clinical reason for a higher dose. They can review it, and if they approve, the order can go in through whatever process your institution requires for exceeding standard limits.\n- **Look at other options**, if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than ibuprofen alone gives. Another agent or a multimodal regimen may work better.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
      }
